        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "They make the king glad with their wickedness, and the princes with their lies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 7:3",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "They are all adulterers, as an oven heated by the baker, who ceaseth from raising after he hath kneaded the dough, until it be leavened.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 7:4",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "In the day of our king the princes have made him sick with bottles of wine; he stretched out his hand with scorners.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 7:5",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "For they have made ready their heart like an oven, whiles they lie in wait: their baker sleepeth all the night; in the morning it burneth as a flaming fire.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 7:6",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "They are all hot as an oven, and have devoured their judges; all their kings are fallen: there is none among them that calleth unto me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Hosea 7:7",
        "book": "Hosea",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 7
      },
